or B5 or B8 (7 total unshown tiles), which provides better winning probability than keeping J1. The resulting hand maintains the strong W1 terminal pung and two bamboo chows, positioning for patterns like \"Concealed Hand,\" \"Pung of Terminals,\" and potentially \"All Simples\" if completed with B5 or B8.\n\nAnswer: Play J1"}
